### Placeholder Services (During Development)
- **Placeholder.com**: `https://via.placeholder.com/800x1200/E5E7EB/6B7280?text=Dress`
- **Unsplash Random**: `https://source.unsplash.com/800x1200/?dress`
- **Lorem Picsum**: `https://picsum.photos/800/1200`

## 🎯 Image Optimization

Before adding images, optimize them:

### Tools:
1. **TinyPNG**: https://tinypng.com/ (Online compression)
2. **ImageOptim**: https://imageoptim.com/ (Mac app)
3. **Squoosh**: https://squoosh.app/ (Google's web tool)

### Command Line (Using ImageMagick):
```bash
# Install ImageMagick
sudo apt install imagemagick  # Linux
brew install imagemagick      # Mac

# Resize image
magick input.jpg -resize 800x1200 output.jpg

# Compress JPEG (quality 85)
magick input.jpg -quality 85 output.jpg

# Convert to WebP (better compression)
magick input.jpg -quality 80 output.webp
```

## 🔄 Using Images in React Components

### Import from public folder:
```jsx
<img src="/assets/images/products/dresses/dress-party-001.jpg" alt="Party Dress" />
```

### Import directly (for bundling):
```jsx
import dressImage from '@/assets/images/products/dresses/dress-party-001.jpg';
<img src={dressImage} alt="Party Dress" />
```

### Dynamic imports:
```jsx
const getDressImage = (vibe, id) => {
  return `/assets/images/products/dresses/dress-${vibe}-${id}.jpg`;
};

<img src={getDressImage('party', '001')} alt="Dress" />
```

## 📦 Sample Product Data Structure

When adding products to MongoDB, use this structure:

```javascript
{
  name: "Floral Maxi Dress",
  images: [
    {
      url: "/assets/images/products/dresses/dress-party-001.jpg",
      alt: "Front view",
      isPrimary: true
    },
    {
      url: "/assets/images/products/dresses/dress-party-001-back.jpg",
      alt: "Back view",
      isPrimary: false
    }
  ],
  category: "dress",
  vibeTags: ["Party", "Glam"],
  // ...other fields
}
```

## 🎨 Color Reference for Vibes

Use these color schemes when selecting/editing images:

| Vibe | Primary Color | Secondary Color | Mood |
|------|--------------|-----------------|------|
| Party | #f5576c | #ffc371 | Energetic, Bold |
| Wedding | #fcb69f | #ffecd2 | Elegant, Romantic |
| Glam | #8B5CF6 | #EC4899 | Luxurious, Sparkly |
| Cocktail | #3B82F6 | #8B5CF6 | Sophisticated, Chic |
| Casual | #10B981 | #34D399 | Relaxed, Comfortable |
| Brunch | #F59E0B | #FBBF24 | Bright, Fresh |
| Date Night | #EF4444 | #F87171 | Romantic, Intimate |
| Festival | #8B5CF6 | #EC4899 | Vibrant, Fun |

## 📝 Naming Conventions

### Be Consistent:
- Use lowercase
- Use hyphens for spaces
- Include category and identifier
- Add color/variant if needed

### Examples:
```
✅ Good:
- dress-party-floral-001.jpg
- earrings-gold-hoop-001.png
- lipstick-red-matte-001.png

❌ Bad:
- IMG_1234.jpg
- product_image.png
- dress.jpg
```

## 🚀 Quick Start - Add Sample Images

### Option 1: Manual Download
1. Go to Unsplash.com
2. Search for "fashion dress"
3. Download images (800x1200)
4. Rename according to conventions
5. Place in appropriate folders

### Option 2: Using Placeholders (Development)
```jsx
// Temporary placeholder until you get real images
const placeholderImage = (category, width = 800, height = 1200) => {
  return `https://via.placeholder.com/${width}x${height}/E5E7EB/6B7280?text=${category}`;
};

<img src={placeholderImage('Dress')} alt="Product" />
```

## 📏 Image Size Budget

Keep total image sizes reasonable:

| Category | Images | Size per Image | Total Budget |
|----------|--------|----------------|--------------|
| Dresses | 40+ | 150-200 KB | ~8 MB |
| Jewelry | 30+ | 50-100 KB | ~3 MB |
| Cosmetics | 30+ | 50-100 KB | ~3 MB |
| Hero/Vibes | 10 | 200-300 KB | ~3 MB |
| **Total** | **110+** | - | **~17 MB** |

